# Cloudflare runtime variables

Worker environment variables and secrets (`SMTP2GO_API_KEY`, `MAIL_FROM`, `MAIL_TO`, `TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY`, and any others) are set **only** in the Cloudflare dashboard.

- Keep `"keep_vars": true` in `wrangler.jsonc`.
- Never add a `vars` object to `wrangler.jsonc` or `wrangler.toml`.
- Never pass `--var` / `--vars` on deploy except OpenNext’s own skew-protection flag.
- Never deploy with a command that omits keep-vars (dashboard `npx wrangler deploy` already reads `keep_vars` from `wrangler.jsonc`).
- Local secrets stay in `.dev.vars` (gitignored). Do not copy them into git or Wrangler config.
